        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hollis, Brookline, Hillsborough County, New Hampshire\n- Organizations: Hollis/Brookline High School\n- People: Elias \"Coach\" Korcoulis\n- Roles: Cross-country coach, track coach\n- Landmarks: Talbot-Taylor Wildlife Sanctuary, Potanipo Pond, Brookline Covered Bridge\n\nFacts:\n- Elias \"Coach\" Korcoulis was born in 1940 and died on March 4, 2006.\n- Elias \"Coach\" Korcoulis served as the cross-country and track coach for Hollis/Brookline High School in Hollis, New Hampshire, from 1962 until his death.\n- Hollis/Brookline High School is a public school located in Hollis, New Hampshire.\n- Hollis/Brookline High School serves the towns of Hollis and Brookline.\n- Brookline is a town in Hillsborough County, New Hampshire, United States.\n- Brookline is home to the Talbot-Taylor Wildlife Sanctuary, Potanipo Pond, and the Brookline Covered Bridge.",
